% Starter catalog of common old-time jam tunes, for tune identification.
%
% IMPORTANT: these are hand-entered *approximate* settings, not authoritative
% transcriptions. That is acceptable and even appropriate for identification,
% because old-time tunes have no canonical setting -- every player's version
% differs in ornaments and passing notes, and the matcher is built to be robust
% to exactly that (it compares beat-level skeletons under all transpositions).
%
% To identify against a real library, point the matcher at its ABC files:
%     fiddle-transcribe identify recording.m4a --catalog /path/to/library
% Any directory of .abc files, or a single multi-tune ABC tunebook, works.

